      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T13:13:44Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, metapool and MetaSwapUtils creation traces, both historical runtimes, the pool's link references, Saddle's post-mortem, BlockSec's technical analysis, verified contract metadata, and the commit-pinned reproduction. Each exploit swap calls MetaSwap at 0x824dcd7b044d60df2e89b1bb888e66d8bcf41491, which delegatecalls selector 0x98414eed on stale MetaSwapUtils 0x88cc4aa0dd6cf126b00c012dda9f6f4fd9388b17. Its _calculateSwap path omits baseVirtualPrice scaling for the saddleUSD-V2 side, so repeated round trips shift the invariant and extract both pool assets. The metapool's 16,676-byte runtime has hash 0xa437f2f7333013b9026c904cdf4451bcedbab55020998f9b49f607d6831dab18 at deployment and immediately before exploitation and contains ten immutable references to the stale library. The library's 18,838-byte runtime has hash 0x8df6f64f967d30dedb2e16b68d0d6aca93cca2c240a9ce4c6ec0842d7b70640a at its creation, pool deployment, and pre-exploit blocks. Pool deployment is therefore the final code-selection event, giving an age of 11,774,507 seconds. Receipt deltas establish the exact two-asset metapool loss and same-transaction LP-token redemption value."
